{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>Mouth to mouth.</b> I told him to separate from his wife (ibid.), and where did I tell him? At Sinai — ״Go say to them, Return to your tents, and you stand here with Me״ (Deuteronomy 5)." "<b>And vision, and not in riddles.</b> This 'vision' is the vision of speech — that I set out My speech to him in the expression on My face, and I do not close it off to him in riddles, as the matter said to Ezekiel (Ezekiel 17), ״Pose a riddle״ etc. Might you say it is the vision of the Shekhinah? Scripture says (Exodus 33), ״You cannot see My face״ (Sifrei)." "<b>And the likeness of YHWH he beholds.</b> This is the vision from behind, as the matter said (Exodus 33), ״And you shall see My back״ (Sifrei)." "<b>In My servant, in Moshe.</b> It does not say 'in My servant Moshe,' but 'in My servant, in Moshe' — in My servant even if he were not Moshe, in Moshe even if he were not My servant, you should have feared him; all the more so since he is My servant. And a servant of the king is like the king, and you should have said, the king does not love him for nothing. And if you say, I do not recognize his deeds — this is harsher than the first (ibid.)."], :book :numbers, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 12, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:10:34.764762148Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}